      "correct": "4",
      "solution": "**Given:**\n\nIf the numerator of a fraction is increased by 15% and the denominator is decreased by 20%, then the fraction becomes 17/65.\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nLet the numerator of the fraction be N, and the denominator of the fraction be D.\n\nNew numerator = N + (15/100) × N\n\n⇒ (100N + 15N)/100\n\n⇒ 115N/100\n\nNew denominator = D – (20/100) × D\n\n⇒ (100D – 20D)/100\n\n⇒ 80D/100\n\nNew fraction = 115N/80D\n\n⇒ (17/65) = (23N/16D)\n\n⇒ 17 × 16D = 23N × 65\n\n⇒ 272D = 1495N\n\n⇒ N/D = 272/1495\n\n**∴**** The original fraction is 272/1495.**\n\n** [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/ca81259519cadfb2d5350673c220e419e60378e9770ad26512fc8e826a8d93f1.png] __Shortcut Trick__**Calculation:\n\nLet the fraction = P/Q\n\nAccording to the question:\n\n⇒ P~ ×~ 115 \\%over Q ~×~ 80\\% = 17over65 \n\n⇒ P~ ×~23over Q ~×~ 16 = 17over65\n\n⇒ P/Q = (16× 17)/(65 × 23)\n\n⇒ P/Q = 272/1495\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 272/1495.**\n\n2f",
