      "solution": "[IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/ca81259519cadfb2d5350673c220e419e60378e9770ad26512fc8e826a8d93f1.png] __Shortcut Trick__\n\nConvert the given fractions into percentages for a quick and direct comparison.\n\n17/30 ≈ 56.67% and 7/15 ≈ 46.67%\n\n27/50 = 54% and 11/20 = 55%\n\nArranging percentages in descending order: 56.67% > 55% > 54% > 46.67%\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 17/30 > 11/20 > 27/50 > 7/15.**\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/c76c13ba2d2ab46b47f8a931ae621dac081a0cb266b142dc23f58659fac4a466.png] **__Alternate Method__**\n\n**Given:**\n\nFractions: 17/30, 7/15, 27/50, 11/20\n\n**Method Used:**\n\nFind the Least Common Multiple (LCM) of all denominators to convert them into equivalent fractions with a common base.\n\n**Calculations:**\n\n⇒ The denominators are 30, 15, 50, and 20.\n\n⇒ LCM of (30, 15, 50, 20) = 300\n\n⇒ Convert 17/30: (17 × 10) ÷ (30 × 10) = 170/300\n\n⇒ Convert 7/15: (7 × 20) ÷ (15 × 20) = 140/300\n\n⇒ Convert 27/50: (27 × 6) ÷ (50 × 6) = 162/300\n\n⇒ Convert 11/20: (11 × 15) ÷ (20 × 15) = 165/300\n\n⇒ Comparing the numerators: 170 > 165 > 162 > 140\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 17/30 > 11/20 > 27/50 > 7/15.**\n\n [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f13e2ad6582c16aa62a83672e2547ad20a01fddb61962a1acce42eb9a1a99caa.png] **__Additional Information__**\n\nCross-Multiplication Method\n\nTo quickly compare two fractions a/b and c/d, cross multiply. If a × d > b × c, then a/b > c/d.\n\nFraction to Percentage Conversion\n\nMultiplying a fraction by 100 converts it into a percentage, making multi-fraction comparisons visually straightforward.\n\nProper vs Improper Fractions\n\nA proper fraction always has a value less than 1 (Numerator < Denominator), while an improper fraction has a value equal to or greater than 1.\n</p",
